Subject: [PATCH] d3d9: put DirectDraw present sources in host-cached memory

A DirectDraw Blt to the primary reaches the KMD as a Blt present whose
source is the application's off-screen plain surface (patch 0014). On
Venus the KMD carries that out as a CPU copy out of the source's blob
mapping. The KMD maps a blob with the cache type the host reports for it,
and virglrenderer reports device-local, host-visible memory as
write-combined, so the copy read the source uncached. On hosts with an AMD
CPU, whose KVM keeps the guest's memory type, a 1280x720 Blt took 38 ms
even with the destination fixed (KMD patch 0002).

DirectDraw present sources now ask for host-cached memory
(YTTRIUM_GDI_RESOURCE_FLAG_CPU_READBACK), as DiscardRenderTarget resources
and the D3D10/11 path's non-shared BIND_PRESENT resources already do.
D3D9 swapchain back buffers do not need it: with KMD 0002 alone they
present at the refresh rate up to 1280x720.

Evidence: docs/present.md, docs/evidence/present/.
Origin: vmlab-win3d present worker.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Resource.cpp b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Resource.cpp
index ae9ab75..b221c1c 100644
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Resource.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Resource.cpp
@@ -2769,11 +2769,17 @@ D3D9CreateResource(HANDLE hDevice, D3DDDIARG_CREATERESOURCE *data)
             templ.nr_samples = 1;
          templ.nr_storage_samples = templ.nr_samples;
          templ.bind = D3D9PipeBind(data);
-         if (D3D9ResourceIsDDrawPresentSource(device, data))
+         const bool ddraw_present_source =
+            D3D9ResourceIsDDrawPresentSource(device, data);
+         if (ddraw_present_source)
             templ.bind |= PIPE_BIND_RENDER_TARGET | PIPE_BIND_DISPLAY_TARGET |
                           PIPE_BIND_SHARED;
          templ.usage = D3D9PipeUsage(data->Pool);
-         if (yttrium && data->Flags.DiscardRenderTarget)
+         /* A DirectDraw Blt to the primary reaches the KMD as a Blt present,
+          * which the KMD carries out on Venus as a CPU copy out of the
+          * source's blob mapping. Device-local memory is mapped
+          * write-combined, so that copy read the source uncached. */
+         if (yttrium && (data->Flags.DiscardRenderTarget || ddraw_present_source))
             templ.flags |= YTTRIUM_GDI_RESOURCE_FLAG_CPU_READBACK;
          if (msaa_primary)
             templ.bind &= ~PIPE_BIND_DISPLAY_TARGET;
